1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[roaring]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,000
[narrator] Strange beasts

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
and monsters.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Evil haunts.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
“The mysterious unknown.”

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words…

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
are called…

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Hunters.

12
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
[theme song playing]

13
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,000
[Kiriko] Alright! We’ll now take you
straight to the site of the exam.

14
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Oh, wow! Isn’t it incredible
that we all passed?

15
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
[Kurapika] I wouldn’t celebrate just yet.

16
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,000
We’ve merely earned the right
to take the Exam.

17
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,000
[Leorio] It’s progress!

18
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,000
I say that calls for a little celebration!

19
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,000
RIVALS x FOR x SURVIVAL

20
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,000
ZABAN CITY

21
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,000
[narrator]
With the help of the Kiriko Navigators,

22
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Gon and his new friends
arrive in Zaban City

23
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,000
the location of this year’s Hunter Exam.

24
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,000
A Navigator’s main job is to identify
worthy applicants for the Hunter Exam.

25
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:37,000
We’re also responsible
for guiding them to the Exam site.

26
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,000
You see,

27
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
that’s because it’s almost impossible
to find the location

28
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,000
without a Navigator.

29
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,000
[shopkeeper] Who wants a taste?

30
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,000
It’s Zaban’s world famous panda-frog
on a stick!

31
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,000
A delicacy!

32
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
This brooch here was excavated
from Zaban’s underground palace.

33
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,000
It’s a real find.

34
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,000
You know Zaban City

35
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,000
is one shady place.

36
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
[Kurapika]
A city that’s as prosperous as this one

37
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,000
is bound to attract its share
of unsavory characters.

38
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Wow!

39
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
What do you think you’re doing, Gon?
Let’s go!

40
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Right!

41
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,000
[man] Here we are.

42
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,000
I’m pretty sure that’s the building.

43
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Whoa...

44
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,000
[Gon] It’s so tall!

45
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Wow, what a nice place!

46
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,000
[Leorio] So that’s the Exam site, huh?

47
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
And this is the crowd that it draws.

48
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Hunter applicants
from all across the world

49
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,000
congregate here.

50
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
My first shot at the Hunter Exam.

51
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
I wonder if this is how Dad felt!

52
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,000
[Kiriko son] Hey, guys!

53
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,000
-Over here.
-[all three] Huh?

54
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,000
This is it.

55
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,000
GOHAN

56
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
[Leorio]
Come on, you’re messing with us, right?

57
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
It just looks like a regular restaurant.

58
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:20,000
You’re tellin’ me that Hunter applicants
from all over the globe

59
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,000
come to this old dive to take the Exam?

60
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
That’s exactly right.

61
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,000
[all three] Huh?

62
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:29,000
[man] The Hunter Exam attracts
millions of applicants every year.

63
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:32,000
And no one would expect the Exam
to be held here, right?

64
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,000
[Leorio] Good point.

65
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Welcome! Take a seat!

66
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
[man] Is the back room available?

67
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,000
What are you having?

68
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:46,000
The steak combo, please.
The one that’ll make us see the light.

69
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Make it three.

70
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Combo for three, eh?

71
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,000
How do you want ‘em cooked?

72
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Grilled slowly over a low flame
‘til done, please.

73
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Got it. See yourselves to the back room.

74
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,000
[Gon] Mmm...

75
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,000
[man] Okay, wait here.

76
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,000
[Leorio] For what?

77
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Where are all the other applicants

78
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:11,000
-[Gon] I can’t wait for that steak combo!
-[Leorio chuckles]

79
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Gon, that was just the password
to get us inside.

80
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,000
There’s no steak combo.

81
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Okay.

82
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,000
So, we don’t get to eat?

83
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,000
[Kiriko son] Only one in ten thousand.

84
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:23,000
You’re very lucky.

85
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
That’s how many ever make it this far.

86
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Nice job.

87
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,000
You did great for first-timers.

88
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Well. Good luck to you.

89
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Thanks for your help!

90
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:43,000
I hope that next year,
I can help you again.

91
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,000
[bang]

92
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,000
[Leorio] Whoa!

93
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:54,000
It seems this room
is actually an elevator.

94
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,000
That explains it.

95
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,000
That bastard thinks
he’ll see us again next year

96
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,000
because he expects us to fail!

97
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
[Kurapika] Once every three years.

98
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,000
What's that?

99
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,000
It’s how often a rookie passes the Exam.

100
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,000
[Gon] It’s that unusual?

101
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,000
It is.

102
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Some can’t handle it.

103
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,000
It’s too mentally and physically taxing.

104
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
It’s also not too uncommon

105
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:24,000
for veterans to break the rookies so badly
that they never retake the test.

106
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,000
So that’s why people
who want to be Hunters

107
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,000
are willing to risk everything for it.

108
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
You’ve hit the nail right on the head,
my little friend!

109
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:37,000
Being a Hunter means making
more money than anyone in the world!

110
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,000
[Kurapika] Wrong!

111
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:42,000
People become Hunters
to join the world’s most noble profession!

112
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,000
Shut up, goody-goody!

113
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,000
Selfish money grubber!

114
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,000
[Kurapika growls]

115
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Hey, Gon! Listen up!

116
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:54,000
There’s a list of the hundred
richest people every year

117
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:57,000
and every single year, there are
over fifty Hunters who make the list.

118
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,000
That’s more than half!

119
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:05,000
There are some Hunters, sad to say,
who seek treasure and wild game.

120
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,000
But they’re second rate.

121
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:10,000
True Hunters work tirelessly
to maintain order

122
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,000
in society as well as in nature!

123
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Oh, screw that!

124
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,000
Once you’re a Hunter,
it’s free to enter most countries!

125
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,000
And facilities? No charge!

126
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,000
How’s that for benefits, huh?

127
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:25,000
Hunters have many difficult
and important responsibilities

128
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,000
preserving artifacts and species,
catching crooks

129
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
and even apprehending rogue Hunters.

130
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,000
It’s the fame and fortune!

131
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,000
That’s why people want to become Hunters!

132
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:38,000
No, it’s conviction, profound knowledge,
and a sound mind and body!

133
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
Traits that are a true Hunter’s pride!

134
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,000
[both growling]

135
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:45,000
[both] Hey, Gon! Which of us
do you agree with?

136
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,000
[both] What kind of Hunter will you be?

137
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,000
Well, when you put it that way,
I guess I...

138
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,000
[elevator dings]

139
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,000
[Kurapika] I think we’ve arrived.

140
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,000
[Leorio] We’ll finish this later.

141
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
[sighs with relief]

142
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Is it me or is the mood here pretty grim?

143
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:18,000
We saw plenty of other applicants
in the city

144
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,000
but these guys’re different.

145
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,000
Each one of them
is a master in their own right.

146
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,000
‘Scuse me!

147
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Looks like everybody’s really on edge
down here.

148
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,000
[Beans] Hello!

149
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,000
Please take your number badge. Thank you!

150
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,000
[Beans] Here you go!

151
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,000
Here.

152
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,000
Be sure to wear this on your chest
at all times, please.

153
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,000
And be careful not to lose it, okay?

154
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,000
[Tonpa]
Don’t think I’ve seen you boys before!

155
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,000
Yo!

156
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
You can tell it’s our first time here?

157
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,000
[Tonpa] More or less.

158
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:02,000
[grunts]

159
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,000
It’s getting easier.

160
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:08,000
It’s my thirty-fifth attempt,
so it comes with the territory.

161
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,000
[all three]
You’ve tried thirty-five times?

162
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:14,000
I guess you could say
I’m a Hunter Exam veteran.

163
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Not really something to brag about.

164
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,000
Indeed.

165
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:22,000
Anyway, if you have any more questions,
I’d be happy to help.

166
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,000
Thanks a lot!

167
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Oh, by the way, the name’s Tonpa.

168
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,000
Hi, I’m Gon.

169
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:29,000
This is Kurapika and this is Leorio.

170
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,000
You sure have taken the Exam a lot.

171
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:35,000
Are you the only one here
who’s tried a bunch of times

172
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,000
or are there others?

173
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:39,000
I might hold the record,
but yeah, there are others.

174
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,000
For instance…

175
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,000
That guy over there.

176
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,000
Number 255.

177
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Todo, the wrestler.

178
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:50,000
Probably the strongest one here.
And he’s smarter than he looks.

179
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:55,000
Over there is 103.
Bourbon, the snake charmer.

180
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:58,000
He can really hold a grudge,
so try not to get on his bad side.

181
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,000
-[snake hisses]
-[Tonpa] Let’s see now...

182
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Number 191, Bodoro,
the kung fu master.

183
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:07,000
He’s getting old, but he’s still
the best martial artist around.

184
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Then there are the brothers,
Amori, Imori, and Umori.

185
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:15,000
They work great as a team,
so they almost always do really well.

186
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,000
And 384.

187
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:20,000
Geretta, the huntsman.

188
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
He specializes
in killing all kinds of creatures

189
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,000
with his blow dart and club.

190
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:28,000
There are more, but they’ve taken the Exam
the most times.

191
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Oh, wow!

192
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,000
[screaming]

193
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:46,000
[strangled cries of pain]

194
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,000
My. How unusual.

195
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:59,000
Seems this poor man’s arms
have turned into flower petals.

196
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:03,000
Now you see them, now you don’t.

197
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,000
[gasps]

198
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,000
You should be more careful.

199
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:11,000
And do apologize if you bump into someone.

200
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,000
[murmuring]

201
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
Just perfect.
The psychopath is back again.

202
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:18,000
You know that guy?

203
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:21,000
So, does that mean he tried last year?

204
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Number 44, Hisoka, the magician.

205
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:28,000
He was the number one pick
to pass last year’s Exam

206
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:31,000
until he almost killed an Examiner
he didn’t approve of.

207
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
Then what the hell is he doing here?!

208
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:36,000
They’re letting him
retake the Exam after something like that?

209
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Of course, they are.

210
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:41,000
They change the content and Examiners
every year.

211
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,000
And the Examiners choose the new material.

212
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:48,000
The devil himself
could pass the Hunter Exam

213
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
-if the Examiners say it’s okay.
-[evil laughter]

214
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
It’s how the whole thing works.

215
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,000
Anyway, nobody likes the guy.

216
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,000
I’d keep my distance if I were you.

217
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,000
Well, he definitely looks dangerous.

218
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Oh! I almost forgot!

219
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Let’s have a toast to friendship.

220
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,000
Whaddya say?

221
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Hey, thanks! Yeah, don’t mind if I do!

222
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,000
I was dying of thirst.

223
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,000
Thanks a lot, buddy!

224
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:17,000
Yeah, thanks a lot!

225
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Thank you.

226
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,000
[examinee]
[chuckles] Well, there he goes.

227
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Playing the nice guy again,
even though he’s the nastiest one here.

228
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
[examinee] Tonpa, the Rookie Crusher

229
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:29,000
[Tonpa]
Here’s to new friends and good fortune.

230
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,000
Cheers!

231
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,000
[chuckles] Sorry, guys.

232
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:41,000
But the juice I gave you
contains a powerful laxative.

233
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:47,000
One sip and your guts will be
on non-stop roller coaster for three days.

234
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:51,000
If you want to take the Exam,
I hope you brought plenty of diapers.

235
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:55,000
[chuckling]

236
00:12:55,000 --> 00:13:01,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

237
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:06,000
LEORIO

238
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,000
[sinister chuckle]

239
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,000
Huh?

240
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Huh?

241
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,000
I think this juice might’ve gone bad,
Mr. Tonpa.

242
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,000
It tastes funny.

243
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:22,000
Seriously?

244
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,000
That was a close call!

245
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,000
Huh? That’s odd.

246
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Real sorry ‘bout that, fellas!

247
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Impossible.

248
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,000
That laxative is flavorless and odorless!

249
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Please forgive me!

250
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:39,000
I had no idea the juice was bad!

251
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,000
[Gon] You don’t have to apologize.

252
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:44,000
What about you? Is your stomach okay?

253
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:47,000
I’m all right. I’m totally fine!

254
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Oh, good!

255
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:51,000
I’ve tried all kinds of plants and grasses
on the mountain back home.

256
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:54,000
So, I can usually taste
when something’s bad.

257
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
That’s some talent you got there!
[nervous chuckle]

258
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Never seen anything like it!

259
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Damn it! He just had to be
some wild mountain kid.

260
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Sorry again.

261
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:07,000
I’ll see you boys around!

262
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Man, I thought he would never shut up.

263
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:15,000
[Tonpa] Something isn’t quite right
about the crop of rookies this year.

264
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:19,000
Like 294. Hanzo.

265
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:23,000
The first time I talked to him,
he actually seemed pretty gullible.

266
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:27,000
Keep this to yourself.

267
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,000
But I am a ninja!

268
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Oh! Is that so?

269
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,000
I seek the legendary scroll. Shhh!

270
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:38,000
It is my secret mission
to track down the Ultimate Ninja Scroll.

271
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,000
That’s why I’m becoming a Hunter.

272
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:44,000
Rumor has it that it’s hidden somewhere
that’s inaccessible to ordinary people.

273
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:49,000
Anyway, this place is pretty boring, huh?

274
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:50,000
I guess so.

275
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:54,000
Hey, we should have a toast.
To friendship and good fortune, eh?

276
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,000
I am a seasoned ninja.

277
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:02,000
I make it a point never to drink anything
offered to me by another.

278
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:05,000
You understand?

279
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:08,000
Oh. Right! Gotcha.

280
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,000
[nervous laughter]

281
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,000
[Tonpa] I can tell he’s no idiot.

282
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:16,000
One wrong move and I could’ve been
in some serious trouble.

283
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,000
-[rattle]
-Huh?

284
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:23,000
[Tonpa] Speaking of trouble, there’s 301.

285
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,000
That guy just oozes danger.

286
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,000
I know one thing;

287
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,000
I’m not going anywhere near him.

288
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:32,000
Then there’s the one I really can’t stand.

289
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,000
187,

290
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,000
Nicholas.

291
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:41,000
Must’ve been tough
to make it this far, huh?

292
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Not really.

293
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:46,000
Everything’s gone
exactly as my data predicted.

294
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:48,000
I used historical data
from past Hunter Exams

295
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:50,000
to calculate this year’s location.

296
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,000
It was really quite simple.

297
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,000
And frankly, rather boring.

298
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:57,000
Oh. Well, good.

299
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:59,000
Impressive work, there, kid.

300
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,000
The name’s Tonpa.
It’s real nice to meet you!

301
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:03,000
Tonpa, is it?

302
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Ah! There you are.

303
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,000
This is your thirty-fifth attempt.

304
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,000
That’s the second highest number
of attempts by anyone!

305
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,000
But it says here

306
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
that you do hold the current record

307
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,000
for the most consecutive attempts
with 30.

308
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:18,000
That’s quite impressive!

309
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Thank you! But it’s no big deal.

310
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:23,000
Whaddya say? Ya wanna toast to friendship?

311
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,000
But after thirty-five attempts

312
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:28,000
you have yet
to successfully pass the Exam.

313
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:34,000
And so, I assume you’re too focused
on your “other” objective.

314
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,000
Am I right, Tonpa the Rookie-Crusher?

315
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,000
Say what?!

316
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:46,000
Fear not. I won’t divulge my findings
with anyone else.

317
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Consider it a prize
for your consecutive appearance record.

318
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,000
Farewell.

319
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,000
[growls]

320
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:01,000
[Tonpa] Just wait, you little bastard.

321
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:05,000
I’m the one who’s gonna break
that snotty nose of yours.

322
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,000
[Killua] Hey! Mr. Tonpa!

323
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:11,000
That juice was great. Got any more?

324
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:14,000
I don’t know if I’m just nervous
but I really am thirsty!

325
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:17,000
Oh! Of course!

326
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:20,000
What the hell?!

327
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:23,000
That laxative he drank
should have taken effect by now!

328
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,000
What’s up with this kid?

329
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:35,000
It’s only a laxative, but still…

330
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:39,000
If the kid drinks that much,
he could die of dehydration.

331
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:42,000
[Killua] Worried?

332
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,000
Well, don’t be. I’ll be fine.

333
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,000
I’ve trained for this.

334
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Poisons don’t hurt me.

335
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:53,000
Impossible!

336
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:58,000
That kid was actually able to tell
what was in the juice?

337
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,000
But if he knew…

338
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:01,000
then why the hell did he drink it?

339
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:05,000
Number 99, Killua.

340
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:10,000
Damn. This year’s rookies
are completely insane.

341
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,000
[smirks]

342
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:13,000
But so what?

343
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:17,000
It just means crushing them
will be all the more satisfying.

344
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,000
[bell ringing]

345
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:33,000
[wall rumbles]

346
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,000
Huh?

347
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,000
I apologize for the delay.

348
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,000
Thank you for waiting.

349
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:56,000
The entry period for Hunter applicants
is officially closed.

350
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:59,000
So, with no further ado,

351
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,000
the Hunter Exam will now begin!

352
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:04,000
-[smirks]
-[grunts]

353
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,000
[smirks]

354
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,000
One final word of caution…

355
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:13,000
If you’re short on luck or ability,

356
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:16,000
keep in mind that
there’s a very real chance

357
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,000
you could end up seriously injured.

358
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Death is another distinct possibility.

359
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:21,000
[determined grunt]

360
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,000
If you’re willing
to accept the risks involved,

361
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:27,000
I’ll ask you to follow me now.

362
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:29,000
But for the rest of you

363
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:33,000
kindly exit through the elevator
located behind you.

364
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,000
[theme music playing]

365
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,000
Right, then. Very well.

366
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:49,000
All 404 applicants
will now participate in Phase One.

367
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:11,000
Yeah, I didn’t think anybody
was gonna leave.

368
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,000
But I’d hoped a few
would duck out at least.

369
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:27,000
[Leorio] Whoa. What...?

370
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:30,000
[Gon] I think the people up front
have started running.

371
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,000
[Kurapika]
It’s because he’s picking up the pace.

372
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,000
How rude of me.
I neglected to introduce myself.

373
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:39,000
I am Satotz, your Examiner
for the First Phase of the Exam.

374
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:44,000
It’s my responsibility
to lead all of you to the Second Phase.

375
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,000
Second?

376
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,000
Whatever happened to the First?

377
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,000
The First Phase is already underway.

378
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:54,000
[murmuring]

379
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:57,000
The First Phase is quite simple.

380
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
All you have to do is follow me
to the Second Phase.

381
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,000
So, try to keep up.

382
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:05,000
Follow you? So that’s it?
There’s nothing else?

383
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,000
[Satotz] That’s right.

384
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:09,000
I cannot tell you where
or when you must arrive.

385
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,000
You need only to follow me.

386
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:17,000
I see how it is.

387
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:19,000
This Exam is weird.

388
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:22,000
Sounds a lot like
a basic endurance test to me.

389
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,000
That’s right up my alley.

390
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:27,000
Keep running, pal! I’m right behind ya!

391
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:31,000
[Kurapika] Not knowing how far
we’ll have to run is mentally stressful,

392
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,000
to say nothing of the physical strain.

393
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:38,000
This is a test of our mental fortitude
as well.

394
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:42,000
[narrator] And so amidst a sea
of warriors and villains,

395
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:45,000
the First Phase of the Exam begins.

396
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:52,000
One candidate is disqualified
before the test even gets under way,

397
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:56,000
bringing the total number
of Hunter applicants to 404.

398
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:59,000
[panting]

399
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:02,000
[theme song playing]

400
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:27,000
[Gon] Next time:

401
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:29,000
"Hope x and x Ambition."

402
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:31,000
-Time to go fishin’!
-[Killua] Yeah.
